# AI Assistant Android

This project is a production-oriented Android app skeleton in Kotlin for an AI assistant that can:

- listen to voice commands using the microphone
- speak responses using text-to-speech
- handle call context and call assistance workflows
- read or reply to messages in an SMS-friendly architecture
- learn habits and track routines locally with Room
- connect to an LLM backend with an OpenAI-compatible API

## Architecture

- Jetpack Compose for UI
- ViewModel + StateFlow for app state
- Room for local habit and message persistence
- Retrofit for AI API integration
- VoiceRecognizer + TextToSpeech-compatible hooks for voice interaction

## Important notes

This repository is intentionally a solid starting point and production-minded foundation. It is not a full, Google Play-ready implementation of all permissions and telecom features, because Android imposes strict limitations for default SMS and call handling. In a production build, you should:

- add privacy consent and user control screens
- implement a proper default SMS role flow
- use Android telecom APIs and accessibility/role-based call handling carefully
- add user authentication, encryption, and data retention controls
- store cloud API keys securely using `BuildConfig` or an encrypted backend

## Build

```bash
./gradlew assembleDebug
```

